{"entries":[{"id":"scofield-2ki-1-3","title":"2 Kings 1:3","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Book Introduction - 2 Kings Read first chapter of 2 Kings This book continues the history of the kingdoms to the captivities. It includes the translation of Elijah and the ministry of Elisha. During this period Amos and Hosea prophesied in Israel, and Obadiah, Joel, Isaiah, Micah, Nahum, Habakkuk, Zephaniah, and Jeremiah in Judah. Second Kings is in seven parts: The last ministry and translation of Elijah, 1:1-2:11. The ministry of Elisha from the translation of Elijah to the anointing of Jehu, 2:12-9:10. The reign of Jehu over Israel, 9:11-10:36. The reigns of Athaliah and Jehoash over Judah, 11:1-12:21. The reigns of Jehoahaz and Joash over Israel, and the last ministry of Elisha, 13:1-25. From the death of Elisha to the captivity of Israel, 14:1-17:41. From the accession of Hezekiah to the captivity of Judah, 18:1-25:30. The events recorded in Second Kings cover a period of 308 years. (Ussher) angel (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-1-15","title":"2 Kings 1:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>angel (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-4-1","title":"2 Kings 4:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>fear (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-4-27","title":"2 Kings 4:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":4,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":4,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>vexed Heb. \"bitter.\" 1 Samuel 1:10.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-5-12","title":"2 Kings 5:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Abana Or, Amana.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-5-25","title":"2 Kings 5:25","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>no whither Heb. \"not hither or thither.\"</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-8-16","title":"2 Kings 8:16","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Jehoram Called Joram, 2 Kings 8:21,23,24. began Heb. reigned, i.e. began to reign in consort with his father.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-10-15","title":"2 Kings 10:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Jehonadab Called Jonadab, Jeremiah 35:6,8,10,14,16,18,19.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-14-7","title":"2 Kings 14:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Edom See 2 Chronicles 25:5-16.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-14-21","title":"2 Kings 14:21","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>Azariah Called Uzziah, 2 Chronicles 26:1; Isaiah 1:1.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-14-29","title":"2 Kings 14:29","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>Zachariah After an interregnum of 11 years. 2 Kings 15:8.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-15-1","title":"2 Kings 15:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>Zachariah After an interregnum of 11 years. 2 Kings 15:8.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-15-10","title":"2 Kings 15:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>smote As prophesied, Amos 7:9.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-15-13","title":"2 Kings 15:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":15,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":15,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Uzziah Matthew 1:8,9 called Ozias 2 Kings 15:7 called Azariah.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-17-7","title":"2 Kings 17:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>sinned Cf. Deuteronomy 28:15-68. From this captivity the ten tribes have never been restored to Palestine. A remnant of Judah returned under Zerubbabel, Ezra, and Nehemiah, and individuals out of the ten tribes (called, after the division of Solomon's kingdom, \"Israel\" in the historical books and Prophets, also \"Ephraim\" by the latter) went back, but the national restoration is yet to be fulfilled. See Palestinian Covenant, (See Scofield \"Deuteronomy 30:3\"), Kingdom, 2 Samuel 7:8-17.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-17-33","title":"2 Kings 17:33","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>feared (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-17-36","title":"2 Kings 17:36","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>fear (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-17-39","title":"2 Kings 17:39","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>fear (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-17-41","title":"2 Kings 17:41","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>feared (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-18-1","title":"2 Kings 18:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>feared (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-18-4","title":"2 Kings 18:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>groves (See Scofield \"Deuteronomy 16:21\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-18-5","title":"2 Kings 18:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>trusted (See Scofield \"Psalms 2:12\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-18-11","title":"2 Kings 18:11","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>did carry Times of the Gentiles. 2 Kings 18:9,12; 2 Kings 25:1-21; Luke 21:24; Revelation 16:19.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-19-2","title":"2 Kings 19:2","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Isaiah called Esaias, Luke 3:4.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-19-10","title":"2 Kings 19:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>trustest (See Scofield \"Psalms 2:12\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-19-35","title":"2 Kings 19:35","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":19,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":19,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>angel (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-20-18","title":"2 Kings 20:18","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>they shall Fulfilled. Daniel 1:3.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-21-26","title":"2 Kings 21:26","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Josiah called Josias, Matthew 1:10.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-22-1","title":"2 Kings 22:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":22,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":22,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>Josiah called Josias, Matthew 1:10.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-23-6","title":"2 Kings 23:6","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>grove (See Scofield \"Deuteronomy 16:21\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-23-13","title":"2 Kings 23:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Ashtoreth 2 Kings 23:6,7. (See Scofield \"Judges 2:13\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-23-34","title":"2 Kings 23:34","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>Jehoiakim Called Jakim. Matthew 1:10,11. (See Scofield \"Matthew 1:10\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-24-8","title":"2 Kings 24:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>eighteen Cf. 2 Chronicles 36:9; 1 Corinthians 10:8. (See Scofield \"1 Corinthians 10:8\").</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-24-12","title":"2 Kings 24:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":24,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":24,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>the king Nebuchadnezzar's eighth year. Jeremiah 25:1.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-25-1","title":"2 Kings 25:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>tenth i.e. January.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-25-3","title":"2 Kings 25:3","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>fourth month i.e. July.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-25-4","title":"2 Kings 25:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>And the city Times of the Gentiles. 2 Kings 25:1-21; Daniel 2:29-45; Luke 21:24; Revelation 16:19.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-25-8","title":"2 Kings 25:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>fifth i.e. August.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-25-25","title":"2 Kings 25:25","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>seventh month i.e. October.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-2ki-25-27","title":"2 Kings 25:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"2KI","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>twelfth month i.e. March.</p>"}]}
